-- title:
--   Preimage in B₀ of j(mathsf q^{qℓ'd}) as cyclic quotient j-invariant
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and for an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q}$ and a valuation subring $A$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ the contraction $A_0 :=$ `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` is the induced valuation subring of $k_0$; all unlabelled algebra structures below are over $A_0$.
--
--   **Reduction data at $q$.** A prime $q \ge 5$, a natural number $M' \ne 0$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. the image of $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A$. Further: a finite set $W$ of places of the field `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` $= \mathrm{ResidueField}(A)(j, j_{M'})$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$, with `hW` asserting that $W$ consists exactly of the places satisfying the predicate `IsSupersingularPlace` for $q$ and $M'$ (the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`); the inclusion `hle` of intermediate fields `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'` inside Laurent series over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, where the first is the $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the full level-$M'$ modular function field and the second is the $X_H$-function field for level $q^2M'$ and $H =$ `levelH q M'`, the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$; a constant reduction datum $R_0$ of type `ConstantReduction A ↥(modularFunctionFieldBar M') (modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M')`, that is, a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the generic function field, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the characteristic-$q$ function field whose kernel is the maximal ideal, lying over $A$ in the sense that an element of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ maps into `R₀.integers` exactly when it lies in $A$, compatible with the residue map of $A$, together with a degree-preserving map on places compatible with orders of functions and a scaling clause making every nonzero function have nonzero residue after multiplication by a constant; the compatibility `hR₀` stating that for a Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, this image lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$; and a chosen element $s \in W$.
--
--   **Base field data.** An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q}$, an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$, and the hypotheses that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is Henselian (`hhens`), has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), and that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hκ`).
--
--   **Auxiliary prime and level structure.** A prime $\ell' \ne q$ with $\ell' \ge 3$ and $\ell' \nmid M'$; an element $\xi \in k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity, together with `hιξ`, the existence of a ring homomorphism $k_0 \to \mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell')}$; an intermediate field $K$ of $k_0 \subseteq$ `LaurentSeries ↥k₀` which by `hK` is the $k_0$-base change `laurentBaseChange` of the $X_H$-function field of level $(q\ell')^2M'$ with $H =$ `levelH (q*ℓ') M'`, the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell')^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q\ell')^\times$; an $A_0$-algebra structure on $K$ with $A_0 \to k_0 \to K$ a scalar tower; and a nonzero $j \in K$ whose underlying Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the classical $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157).
--
--   **Functoriality and group-law data.** The hypotheses `hℓ` and `hM` assert, for every $A_0$-algebra $T$, that `IsLevelPStructure · ℓ' ·` is preserved by variable change on a Weierstrass curve together with the induced change `LevelPData.variableChange` of the four coordinates, and that `IsGamma0PowAt · p k ·` is preserved by variable change together with the substitution `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k)` on the kernel polynomial, where `gamma0PowDeg p k` is $1$ if $p^k = 2$ and $\varphi(p^k)/2$ otherwise. Next, a family of relative group laws $\mathcal G$ on the projective models of Weierstrass curves over $A_0$-algebras, assumed chord–tangent (`h𝒢`: the group law is given by a points evaluation) and with the origin as identity (`h𝒢O`: the unit section is cut out by a homomorphism from the origin chart killing $x/y$ and $z/y$); a level transport $\mathcal T$ for $\mathcal G$ at $q$, assumed to be a section transport (`h𝒯`), so that the transported Drinfeld sections $P, Q$ are compatible with variable changes and with coefficient maps. Finally `hVC` and `hCO` provide, for every $A_0$-algebra $T$ (respectively every $A_0$-algebra map $f : T \to T'$) and every projective Weierstrass curve, a graded ring homomorphism between the projective-model graded rings, dominating the irrelevant ideal, which realises the variable change (`IsVariableChangeHom`) respectively the coefficient change (`IsCoefficientHom`).
--
--   **Moduli package and the point $x_0$.** Write $\mathcal R :=$ `rigidDataPow A₀ ℓ' M' q hℓ hM 𝒢 𝒯`, the rigid Weierstrass datum combining the $\Gamma_0$-power component for $M'$, the level-$\ell'$ point component and the Drinfeld level-$q$ component. Given: an absolute level moduli package $P_0$ for $\mathcal R$, i.e. an $A_0$-algebra `P₀.B₀` with a universal point `P₀.univ` such that every point of $\mathcal R$ over an $A_0$-algebra $T$ is the image of `P₀.univ` under a unique $A_0$-algebra map `B₀ → T`; a point $x_0$ of $\mathcal R$ over $K$ whose $j$-invariant `jOf x₀`, read in `LaurentSeries ↥k₀`, equals `jqNModC k₀ (q*ℓ')`, the $q$-expansion of $j$ in $\mathsf q^{q\ell'}$ (`hx₀`); and an $A_0$-algebra map `clC` from `P₀.B₀` to the chart algebra `chartAlgFin A₀ K j` of elements of $K$ integral over $A_0[j]$, whose composite into $K$ is the classifying map `P₀.classify x₀` (`hclC`).
--
--   **The Tate pin `hμ`.** This hypothesis asserts the existence of a variable change $C$ over `LaurentSeries ↥k₀` and a raw point $r$ of $\mathcal R$ over $K$ such that: (i) the class of $r$ is $x_0$; (ii) writing $(x_\infty, y_\infty)$ for `cuspPoint k₀ (q*ℓ')` at the unit attached to $\xi$ and the vector $(1,0)$, one has $C.u\,(2x_\infty + 1/6) = 2y_\infty + x_\infty$, $C.r = -1/12$, $C.s = -1/2$, $C.t = 1/24$; (iii) the curve of $r$, pushed to `LaurentSeries ↥k₀`, equals $C \cdot$ `tateBase k₀ (q*ℓ')`; (iv) for each prime $p \mid M'$, each field $F'$ with a ring homomorphism $f : k_0 \to F'$ and each primitive $p^{v_p(M')}$-th root of unity $\zeta \in F'$, the $\Gamma_0$-component polynomial `r.level.1 p`, pushed to `LaurentSeries ↥k₀` and then reduced coefficientwise along $f$, equals `kernelVariableChangeDeg` of $C$ (with degree `gamma0PowDeg p (M'.factorization p)`) applied to $\prod_a (X - x(\zeta^a))$, the product over $1 \le a \le p^{v_p(M')}/2$ with $p \nmid a$ of the linear factors in the first coordinates of `toricPoint F' (q*ℓ') (ζ^a)`; (v) the level-$\ell'$ datum `r.level.2.1`, pushed to `LaurentSeries ↥k₀`, equals the $C$-variable change of `cuspData k₀ (q*ℓ')` at the unit attached to $\xi$ and the vectors $(q,0)$, $(0,-q)$ in $\mathbb Z/q\ell'$; (vi) there exist $P_x, P_y, Q_x, Q_y \in K$ whose Laurent images are the four coordinates `xP, yP, xQ, yQ` of the $C$-variable change of `cuspData k₀ (q*ℓ')` at the same unit and the vectors $(\ell',0)$, $(0,-\ell')$, and the Drinfeld sections `r.level.2.2.P` and `r.level.2.2.Q` pass through $(P_x,P_y)$ and $(Q_x,Q_y)$ in the sense of `IsSectionThrough`.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses, for every nonzero natural number $d$ dividing $M'$, and given that `jqNModC k₀ (q*ℓ'*d)` lies in $K$ (`hcK`) and that the resulting element of $K$ lies in the chart algebra `chartAlgFin A₀ K j` (`hcC`), there exists $c \in$ `P₀.B₀` with the following two properties.
--
--   First, `clC c` is that element, namely `jqNModC k₀ (q*ℓ'*d)` regarded in the chart algebra.
--
--   Second, for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ with an $A_0$-algebra structure, every $A_0$-algebra map $\varphi :$ `P₀.B₀` $\to \Omega$ which annihilates every $b'$ with `clC b' = 0` (`hφ`), with $M'$ invertible in the sense that its image in $\Omega$ is nonzero (`hM'Ω`), every raw point $x_\Omega$ of $\mathcal R$ over $\Omega$ whose class is the image of the universal point `P₀.univ` under $\varphi$ (`hxΩ`), and every point $g$ of the affine curve of $x_\Omega$ satisfying the two clauses of `hg` — that $g$ has additive order exactly $M'$, and that for each prime $p \mid M'$, each $n$ and each nonsingular affine point $(x_1,y_1)$ with $n \cdot g = (x_1,y_1)$ and $n \cdot g$ of additive order $p^{v_p(M')}$, the element $x_1$ is a root of the $\Gamma_0$-component polynomial `xΩ.level.1 p` — one has
--   $$\varphi(c) = \mathrm{cyclicQuotientJ}\,(x_\Omega.\mathrm{curve})\,\bigl(\mathbb Z \cdot ((M'/d) \cdot g)\bigr)\,d,$$
--   the quantity $c_4^3/\Delta$ of the cyclic quotient curve of $x_\Omega.\mathrm{curve}$ by the subgroup generated by $(M'/d) \cdot g$, taken with parameter $d$.
--
--   This is the étale case of the computation identifying, for each divisor $d$ of $M'$, a distinguished element of the representing ring $B_0$ of the rigid level-$(\Gamma_0(M'), \ell'\text{-points}, \text{Drinfeld }q)$ moduli problem: the element whose image in the chart algebra is the $q$-expansion $j(\mathsf q^{q\ell'd})$, and whose value at a geometric point where $M'$ is invertible is the $j$-invariant of the quotient of the fibre by the order-$d$ subgroup cut out by the $\Gamma_0(M')$-data, as given by Vélu's formulae. It is proved by combining the existence of the preimage over the chart algebra with the evaluation of $j(\mathsf q^{q\ell'd})$ at the Tate point pinned by `hμ`, and it feeds the corresponding statement for powers and level automorphisms used in the degeneracy analysis of the modular curve at the supersingular places above $q$.
